I have been following Stonehearth since Alpha 10 and after 17 hours of game I feel confortable enough to share my opinion with you guys. I'm going to do a list of Pro and Con, I hope you enjoy it.
Ps:. Remember this game is in ALPHA stage so I can't avaliate everything, because it is constantly changing.
Pros:
- Game is constantly updated (weekly);
- You can follow the game's development in Stonehearth's Website, Twitch Tv or in their Youtube Channel;
- The team is always helpful and you can contact them in their own Forum or in Steam's Forum;
- The game has an original cube style which is kind of criative and cool;
- Stonehearth is pretty complete for an Alpha version;
- The game has gorgeous graphics for an Alpha state;
- The animations are pretty good;
- We have nice bosses and monsters;
- Building mechanics are good and you can basically create everything you want;
- You have a lot of crafting options ( Carpenter, Blacksmith, Herbalist....etc). Therefore you need to update them;
- The furniture of the game is just amazing;
- You have three different difficult modes (Peaceful, Normal, Hardcore);
- The game is always challenging although you play in normal mode; < Disregarding the Peaceful mode.
- Hardcore mode is really amazing and challenging; < ( my favorite part )
- You have a nice story although it's kind of silly;
- The combat in the game is really nice. You have 4 different classes in combat ( Tank, Ranger, Cleric, DPS );
- You have 2 biomes to play ( Desert, Florest ) and they are creating more + season system;
- You have at now 2 different "races" to play;
- The game's community is active.
Con:
- The game still having some bugs(Buildings/Combat), but it's in Alpha stage. It will change with the time;
- The music is nice, but after a while it feels monotonus. I hope they put more soundtracks soon;
- The combat's system is really great, but their auto-attack make it harder to play. I hope it's just a question of time to their change it;
- The "races" seems predetermined for each biome which is a pity. Maybe they can change that;
- The citizens also delay a lot to build something;
- By the way, the game is not really optimized which means more work for your hardware(>> RAM <<);
- Water bugs <<< It's really annoying but I bet it will change with the time.
It's everything that I could see about this game. The game is fantastic, I personaly love it. I would recomend it for almost everybody. But remember, this game is Alpha Stage which means that you will find bugs. I recommend this game for people that have patience and understand that this current stage is going to be improved slowly.
Ps:. Before you buy this game give a look at their website and on their development map. So you can catch up what they are working in.
My Opinion:
The game have a great potential for turn the best sandbox construction game after Dwarf Fortress. I personally had a great time playing Stonehearth. Building your own castles, Keeps, collecting resorcess, constructing a solid economy and defending your town against strong Trolls and goblings is pretty nice and cool guys! I had played other games before Stonehearth such as Towns, Craft the World, Terraria, Timberstone and Dwarf Fortress. I can assure you guys that no game is like Stonehearth. No game mix RPG + RTS + SANDBOX so well as this game and this is because I love it!
Ps:. Remember this review was wrote in Alpha 17. So, the game can be better or worse after some updates.
Ps2:. The game is on development I can't review it completely for that.

